{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfpkmGk5U8AVzavqVnrvF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The assertion fails once the poll timeout expires. `expect.poll` doesn't wait forever on a hanging callback. It races each call against the overall deadline, so a promise that never settles ends the poll at the timeout. The test then fails with a timeout error. In Playwright, the message looks like \"Timeout 5000ms exceeded while waiting on the predicate\" and includes the custom message if you gave one. The default timeout is the expect timeout (5s in Playwright, 1s in Vitest's `expect.poll`), and you can override it with `{ timeout }`.\n\nThe pending promise isn't cancelled, though. Any side effects it has may keep running in the background, so make the callback itself time-bounded if that matters."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2243,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2243},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"269f6df4-f994-4df2-be4d-34fe0b9b0cdd","uuid":"f14ba5dc-8bdc-4cbe-9b79-e7131ba5047a","timestamp":"2026-10-08T12:17:21.989Z","request_id":"req_011CfpkmGWgkJTMMpEMr5gDH"}
